
# ANALOG CABLE CONDITION ASSESSMENT AND FAULT INDICATION SYSTEM

## Project Overview
This project is designed to assess cable conditions and indicate faults using an analog electronic circuit based on the LM358 operational amplifier.

The system uses voltage sensing and comparator circuits to identify abnormal cable conditions and provide visual indications through LEDs.

## Main Components
- LM358 Operational Amplifier
- Resistors
- Capacitors
- LEDs
- Potentiometer
- DC Power Supply
- Test Cable

## Working Principle
1. A low-voltage test signal is applied to an isolated cable.
2. The sensing circuit measures the cable response.
3. The LM358 processes the analog signal.
4. The comparator section checks the signal against a reference voltage.
5. LEDs indicate the detected cable condition.

## Fault Indications
- Green LED - Normal Condition
- Red LED - Fault Condition
- Yellow LED - Abnormal Condition

## Technologies
- Analog Electronics
- LM358 Operational Amplifier
- Voltage Sensing
- Comparator Circuit

## Applications
- Cable condition monitoring
- Electrical maintenance
- Basic cable fault identification
- Educational electronics projects

## Project Type
Analog Electronics Project

## Controller
LM358 Operational Amplifier

No Arduino or ESP32 is used.

## Safety
Use only an isolated, current-limited low-voltage test supply. Never connect the prototype directly to mains electricity.
